round college football for Week 12.","published":"2026-11-19T11:45:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50513003/college-football-odds-best-bets-week-12-spreads-lines-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"South Carolina star QB LaNorris Sellers set to play vs. No. 1 Georgia","description":"South Carolina star QB LaNorris Sellers is set to play in Saturday's game vs. No. 1 Georgia after not appearing on the injury report Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-19T03:01:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50526154/south-carolina-qb-lanorris-sellers-set-play-vs-georgia","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NC State names NFL assistant Jason Michael as OC under Philip Rivers","published":"2026-11-19T12:21:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50524698/nc-state-names-nfl-assistant-michael-oc-rivers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia AG asks SEC to take action against LSU's 'contempt for the rules'","description":"The Georgia Attorney General blasted LSU in a letter to SEC commissioner Greg Sankey, encouraging sanctions against the Tigers, \"up to and including expulsion.\"","published":"2026-11-19T04:59:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50524054/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5031157/reed-harris","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":46,"round":2,"team":"LV","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Reed Harris (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:29Z","intro":"Reed Harris is an American football wide receiver for the Arizona State Sun Devils. He previously played for the Boston College Eagles.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Harris was born in Minnesota, and moved to Conrad, Montana when he was a year old, growing up on a 12,000 acre farm. Harris moved to Great Falls, Montana when he was in 8th grade, later attending Great Falls High School where he was the football team's starting quarterback as a sophomore and junior. He moved to wide receiver during his senior season and finished with 553 yards and three touchdowns. Harris finished his high school career completing 229 passes for 21 touchdowns, while adding 1,575 yards and 13 touchdowns on the ground, with 36 receptions for 536 yards and four touchdowns through the air. He also added 83 tackles with ten being for a loss, nine sacks, five fumble recoveries, and a forced fumble on defense. Coming out of high school, Harris was rated as a three-star recruit in football, basketball, and track by 247Sports, and was ranked as the top player in the state of Montana in the class of 2023. He committed to play college football for the Boston College Eagles over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Oregon State, Montana, Montana State, Colorado State, Utah State, San Diego State, Central Michigan, Harvard, Idaho, and Idaho State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"BOSTON COLLEGE\nAs a freshman in 2023, Harris appeared in four games, making one catch, as he was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2024 season, he caught his first career touchdown in a win over Duquesne. During the 2024 season, Harris played in all 13 games with 11 starts, catching 17 passes for 486 yards and four touchdowns. During the 2025 season, he totaled 39 catches for 673 yards and five touchdowns; after the conclusion of the season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal."}]}}